# Path classes for a review brief. A line's class decides whether the
# triage sees it at all: every class here but `harness` is Counted (file
# names and line counts on the page, no diff body).
#
# One per line: <class> <glob>. Classes: generated, lockfile, docs, test,
# harness. Precedence in the program: harness, then generated (also by an
# `@generated` / `Code generated ... DO NOT EDIT` marker in a file's first
# five lines), lockfile, docs, test, then live. Inline `#[cfg(test)]` items
# and files declared by `#[cfg(test)] mod` are found by the program, not
# listed here.

# Test support is read as code, at least Glance: a harness change can
# weaken every test with no weakening signal.
harness crates/testkit/
harness **/fault_provider.rs
harness **/*test_double*.rs
harness **/*test_support*.rs

generated gen/

lockfile Cargo.lock
lockfile **/go.sum
lockfile devenv.lock
lockfile flake.lock

docs **/*.md
docs docs/

test **/tests/
test **/testdata/
test **/benches/
test crates/e2e/
test crates/bin-e2e/
test crates/plugingo-e2e/
test crates/plugin-entrypoint-test-cdylib/
